  "notes": "Describes surfaces, coatings, or skin coming off naturally or as a result of damage. As an intransitive verb, the peeling happens on its own without someone actively removing it.\n\nTRANSITIVE PAIR:\n- {剥|む}ける (intransitive) — to peel off (by itself)\n- ⟦{剥|む}く→剥く：02305_muku⟧ (transitive) — to peel (something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{皮|かわ}→皮：02187_kawa⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{剥|む}ける — skin peels\n- ⟦ペンキ→ペンキ：00342_penki⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{剥|む}ける — paint peels off\n- ⟦{塗装|とそう}→塗装：06582_tosou⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{剥|む}ける — coating peels off\n\nCONTRAST WITH {剥|は}がれる:\n- {剥|む}ける — for thin layers like skin, bark, paint\n- ⟦{剥|は}がれる→剥がれる：04363_hagareru⟧ — for things stuck or attached coming off (labels, stickers, wallpaper)",
